IMPORT prelude

-- Energy Market Authority of Singapore Act 2001 (Singapore) -- the decision rules of the Authority: its constitution (s 5), the
-- protection of its people from suit (s 11), borrowing (s 12), withdrawals from the Future Energy Fund (s 19A), the rate to recover
-- the costs of energy initiatives (s 19B), the Act's offences and their penalties (ss 20, 27, 28, 29), composition (s 30), the
-- Minister's approvals (ss 12, 19A(3), 30(2), 31, Second Schedule), and membership, quorum, voting and delegation (First Schedule).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EMASA2001.txt. The deposit says
-- it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; later amendments are annotated in the body, the latest being
-- Act 27 of 2024 (s 19B, in force 1 July 2025; s 5(1), in force 31 March 2025; ss 19, 19A, in force 8 November 2024).
-- The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body (it lists 19A, 19B and 20 against the wrong
-- headings); the body's numbering is followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. It is an institutional Act, so this row takes the
-- rules with decision content. Not encoded: the functions in s 6 (non-justiciable, s 6(3)), Ministerial directions (s 8), the
-- Chief Executive and staff (s 9), the financial housekeeping in ss 13 to 18, the Fund's composition (s 19), the transfer from the
-- Public Utilities Board in Part 4 (ss 21 to 26), the enforcement powers in s 27(1) beyond the offence they support, sealing,
-- salaries and procedure in the First Schedule, and the amount of any s 19B rate (left to regulations, none retrieved).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Energy Market Authority of Singapore Act 2001 -- the Authority`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` GREATER THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `5 -- constitution`

-- s 5(1): "The Authority consists of the following members: (a) a Chairperson; (b) 5 or more other members as the Minister may from
-- time to time determine." [Act 27 of 2024 wef 31/03/2025]
GIVEN `has a Chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority is constituted as section 5 requires` IF
    `has a Chairperson` AND `number of other members` AT LEAST 5

§§ `11 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 11: "No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie against any member, officer or employee of the Authority or other person
-- acting under the direction of the Authority for anything which is in good faith done or intended to be done in the execution or
-- purported execution of this Act or any other written law."
GIVEN `is a member, officer, employee or person directed by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in the execution or purported execution of written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is protected from suit` IF
        `is a member, officer, employee or person directed by the Authority`
    AND `acted in good faith`
    AND `in the execution or purported execution of written law`

§§ `12 -- power to borrow`

-- s 12(1): the Authority "cannot raise loans ... except in accordance with this section". (2) by (a) mortgage, overdraft or other
-- means; (b) charge on property or revenue; or (c) "debentures or bonds, or such other instrument as the Minister may approve".
-- (3) loans may be raised "(a) from the Government; or (b) with the approval of the Minister, from another source, whether in or
-- outside Singapore".
DECLARE Lender IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `a bank in Singapore`
    `a lender outside Singapore`

DECLARE `Means of borrowing` IS ONE OF
    `a mortgage or overdraft`
    `a charge on property or revenue`
    `debentures or bonds`
    `another instrument`

GIVEN `the lender` IS A Lender,
      `the means` IS A `Means of borrowing`,
      `the Minister approved the source` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister approved the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the loan may be raised` IF
        (    `the lender` EQUALS `the Government`
         OR  `the Minister approved the source`)
    AND (    (NOT (`the means` EQUALS `another instrument`))
         OR  `the Minister approved the instrument`)

§§ `19A -- withdrawals from the Future Energy Fund`

-- s 19A(1): moneys "may be withdrawn by the Authority only for the following purposes": (a) carrying on or financially supporting a
-- low-carbon energy project or energy supply security project; (b) preparatory studies; (c) land acquisition costs and compensation
-- for such a project; (d) insurance premiums on Fund-financed assets; (e) amounts relating to the sale, disposal or write-off of
-- Fund investments; (f) investing under s 15; (g) the Fund's setting-up and administration expenses.
-- (3): "No investment paid for with moneys from the Future Energy Fund may be written-off by the Authority without the prior approval
-- of the Minister."
-- (4): the moneys "must not be withdrawn -- (a) for the purposes of land reclamation by or on behalf of the Government; (b) to pay for
-- any fuel used for the generation of any electricity; or (c) to pay for any recurrent costs" of a project.
-- (2): for a project "commenced before the appointed date", withdrawal is allowed only if, before that date, the project's
-- infrastructure, property or system "is not in a position to be used to provide goods or services to any person".
-- INFERENCE: (2) is applied to the project-related purposes, (a) to (d); it is not applied to investing or administration.
-- INFERENCE: (3) is applied to a withdrawal under (1)(e) for a write-off.
DECLARE `Fund purpose` IS ONE OF
    `building a low-carbon energy project`
    `building an energy supply security project`
    `preparatory studies for a project`
    `land acquisition costs for a project`
    `insurance premiums on Fund-financed assets`
    `writing off a Fund investment`
    `investing under section 15`
    `Fund administration expenses`
    `land reclamation for the Government`
    `fuel for generating electricity`
    `recurrent costs of a project`
    `the Authority's general running costs`

DECLARE Withdrawal HAS
    `purpose` IS A `Fund purpose`
    `the Minister gave prior approval to the write-off` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the project commenced before the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the project could serve anyone before the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `Fund purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose relates to a project` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `building a low-carbon energy project` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `building an energy supply security project` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `preparatory studies for a project` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `land acquisition costs for a project` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `insurance premiums on Fund-financed assets` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `Fund purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is listed in section 19A(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `land reclamation for the Government` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `fuel for generating electricity` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `recurrent costs of a project` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Authority's general running costs` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the withdrawal` IS A Withdrawal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the withdrawal is permitted` IF
        `the purpose is listed in section 19A(1)` (`the withdrawal`'s `purpose`)
    AND (    (NOT (`the withdrawal`'s `purpose` EQUALS `writing off a Fund investment`))
         OR  `the withdrawal`'s `the Minister gave prior approval to the write-off`)
    AND (    (NOT (`the purpose relates to a project` (`the withdrawal`'s `purpose`)))
         OR  (NOT (`the withdrawal`'s `the project commenced before the appointed date`))
         OR  (NOT (`the withdrawal`'s `the project could serve anyone before the appointed date`)))

-- s 19A(6): an "energy supply security project" is one "to ensure the security and reliability of any supply of energy utilities in
-- Singapore, necessitated by any low-carbon energy project", including transmission and distribution upgrades and power back-up:
-- "(i) energy storage systems; (ii) fast-response generators (including diesel generators and gas engines) ...; (iii) systems
-- activating localised generators ...; and (iv) combined-cycle gas turbines".
DECLARE `Back-up asset` IS ONE OF
    `an energy storage system`
    `a diesel generator`
    `a gas engine`
    `a combined-cycle gas turbine`
    `a grid upgrade`
    `a coal-fired power station`

GIVEN `the asset` IS A `Back-up asset`, `necessitated by a low-carbon energy project` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an energy supply security project` IF
        `necessitated by a low-carbon energy project`
    AND CONSIDER `the asset`
        WHEN `a coal-fired power station` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `19B -- rates to recover the cost of energy initiatives`

-- s 19B(1): the section applies to an energy initiative "(a) to ensure the security or reliability of the supply of any energy
-- utilities; (b) to improve or enhance the operation of any market ...; (c) to lower carbon emissions in connection with the supply
-- of any energy utilities". (4)(a): the persons who must pay are any of "(i) any electricity licensee ... or any person exempted
-- from the requirement of an electricity licence"; (ii) the same for gas; (iii) the same for district cooling; "(iv) any consumer of
-- any energy utilities", "whether or not the person derives any direct or immediate benefit". (5): a rate for one utility may be
-- payable by licensees or consumers "in relation to that or any other energy utilities".
-- INFERENCE: a payer outside the four classes cannot be made to pay; "gas" excludes liquefied petroleum gas (s 2).
DECLARE `Initiative aim` IS ONE OF
    `security or reliability of supply`
    `improving an energy market`
    `lowering carbon emissions in supply`
    `promoting the Authority's public image`

DECLARE Payer IS ONE OF
    `an electricity licensee`
    `a person exempted from an electricity licence`
    `a gas licensee`
    `a district cooling licensee`
    `a household consumer of electricity`
    `an LPG cylinder dealer as such`

GIVEN `the aim` IS AN `Initiative aim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 19B covers the initiative` IF
    CONSIDER `the aim`
    WHEN `promoting the Authority's public image` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the aim` IS AN `Initiative aim`, `the payer` IS A Payer, `the payer benefits directly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payer may be made to pay the rate` IF
        `section 19B covers the initiative` `the aim`
    AND CONSIDER `the payer`
        WHEN `an LPG cylinder dealer as such` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 19B(7), (8): amounts recovered "are to be applied to meet the costs" of the initiative; where they "exceed the costs", the
-- Authority "may retain the excess and apply the excess in payment of the costs of any other energy initiative".
GIVEN `amount recovered` IS A NUMBER, `cost of the initiative` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excess the Authority may retain for other initiatives` MEANS
    `the larger of` (`amount recovered` MINUS `cost of the initiative`) 0

§§ `20 -- the Authority's symbol`

-- s 20(2): "Any person who uses a symbol or representation identical with that of the Authority, or which so resembles the
-- Authority's symbol or representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion" commits
-- an offence: "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both and, in the case of a
-- continuing offence, ... a further fine not exceeding $250 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- conviction".
GIVEN `uses an identical symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `uses a symbol likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the symbol use is an offence` IF
    `uses an identical symbol` OR `uses a symbol likely to deceive or confuse`

GIVEN `days or part days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for the symbol offence` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 250 TIMES `days or part days continued after conviction`

`the maximum imprisonment in months for the symbol offence` MEANS 12

§§ `27 -- obstructing the Authority's officers`

-- s 27(2): an offence where a person "(a) refuses to give access to, or assaults, obstructs, hinders or delays, an officer"; "(b)
-- wilfully misstates or without lawful excuse refuses to give any information or ... to produce any book, document"; or "(c) fails
-- to comply with a lawful demand". Penalty: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or
-- ... both".
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `obstructing an officer`
    `refusing an officer access`
    `wilfully misstating information`
    `refusing information`
    `ignoring a lawful demand`
    `innocently misstating information`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under section 27` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `refusing information` THEN NOT `had a lawful excuse`
    WHEN `innocently misstating information` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

`the maximum fine under section 27` MEANS 5000

§§ `28 -- secrecy`

-- s 28(1): a person "who is or has been a member, an officer, an employee or an agent of the Authority or a member of a committee"
-- must not, "except for the purpose of the performance of A's duties ... or when lawfully required to do so by any court or where
-- required or allowed by the provisions of any written law, disclose any information relating to the affairs of the Authority or of
-- any other person which has been obtained by A in the performance of A's duties". (2): $5,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `by a present or former insider` IS A BOOLEAN
    `information obtained in the course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for the performance of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lawfully required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `required or allowed by written law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence under section 28` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `by a present or former insider`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `information obtained in the course of duties`
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `for the performance of duties`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `lawfully required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `required or allowed by written law`)

§§ `29 -- officers of bodies corporate`

-- s 29: where a body of persons commits an offence "with the authority, consent or connivance of any person who ... was a director,
-- manager, secretary or other similar officer or a partner ... or was purporting to act in any such capacity, that person shall also
-- be guilty of that offence".
GIVEN `the body committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was an officer or partner or purported to be` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `authorised, consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the body committed an offence under this Act`
    AND `was an officer or partner or purported to be`
    AND `authorised, consented or connived`

§§ `30 -- composition`

-- s 30(1): the Authority "may compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting ... a
-- sum not exceeding $3,000". (2): the offences are prescribed by regulations made "with the approval of the Minister".
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum to collect` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for that sum` IF
    `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum to collect` AT MOST 3000

§§ `12, 19A(3), 30(2), 31 and Second Schedule -- what needs the Minister's approval`

-- s 12(3)(b): borrowing from a source other than the Government. s 19A(3): writing off a Fund investment. ss 30(2), 31: making
-- regulations. Second Schedule para 1(b): forming a company "for such other purposes as may be approved by the Minister" (para 1(a),
-- to carry out the Authority's functions, needs none); para 1A: constructing, acquiring or leasing property (no approval); para 2:
-- "To sell, with the approval of the Minister, any immovable property".
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `borrowing from the Government`
    `borrowing from a bank`
    `writing off a Future Energy Fund investment`
    `making regulations`
    `forming a company to carry out the Authority's functions`
    `forming a company for another purpose`
    `acquiring or leasing property`
    `selling immovable property`

GIVEN `the act` IS AN Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act needs the Minister's approval` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `borrowing from the Government` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `forming a company to carry out the Authority's functions` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `acquiring or leasing property` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `First Schedule -- members, meetings and delegation`

-- para 5: "A member may resign his or her office at any time by giving not less than one month's notice to the Minister."
GIVEN `months of notice given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resignation notice is sufficient` IF
    `months of notice given` AT LEAST 1

-- para 8: no person may be appointed or continue as a member who "(a) is an undischarged bankrupt or has made any arrangement with
-- the person's creditors; (b) has been sentenced to imprisonment for a term exceeding 6 months and has not received a free pardon;
-- or (c) is incapacitated by physical or mental illness".
GIVEN `is an undischarged bankrupt or has a creditors' arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER,
      `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is incapacitated by illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is disqualified from membership` IF
        `is an undischarged bankrupt or has a creditors' arrangement`
    OR  (`months of imprisonment sentenced` GREATER THAN 6 AND (NOT `received a free pardon`))
    OR  `is incapacitated by illness`

-- para 6(b): the office becomes vacant "if he or she fails to attend 3 consecutive meetings of the Authority without sufficient
-- cause (the sufficiency of which is to be decided by the Authority)".
GIVEN `consecutive meetings missed` IS A NUMBER, `the Authority accepted the cause as sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office is vacated for absence` IF
    `consecutive meetings missed` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT `the Authority accepted the cause as sufficient`)

-- para 11(1): "The quorum at every meeting of the Authority is one-third of the total number of members in office or 3 members,
-- whichever is the higher". (3): "a simple majority of the members present and voting except that, in the case of an equality of
-- votes, the Chairperson of the meeting has a casting vote in addition to the Chairperson's original vote".
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `members in office` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a quorum is present` IF
    `members present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `members in office` AND `members present` AT LEAST 3

GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER,
      `members in office` IS A NUMBER,
      `votes for` IS A NUMBER,
      `votes against` IS A NUMBER,
      `the chair casts the deciding vote for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is adopted` IF
        `a quorum is present` `members present` `members in office`
    AND (    `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
         OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `the chair casts the deciding vote for`))

-- para 14(2), (3): the Authority may delegate "all or any of the powers, functions and duties ... except the powers to prescribe or
-- levy dues and rates and borrow money".
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `licensing decisions`
    `compounding offences`
    `withdrawing from the Future Energy Fund`
    `prescribing or levying dues and rates`
    `borrowing money`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power may be delegated` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `prescribing or levying dues and rates` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `borrowing money` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
